# Lint verification

When a Gradle project has Spotless, PMD, SpotBugs or CodeNarc configured in
`build.gradle`:

1. Before reporting a change as done, run `./gradlew spotlessApply`, then
   `./gradlew check`. In a Grails app, `./gradlew check -x integrationTest` is
   acceptable when no database is available; say that you skipped them.
2. Fix violations in the code. Lint does not run in CI, so this run is the only
   gate.
3. Suppress only a deliberate exception, at the narrowest scope (line, then
   method, never class), with a one-line reason next to it.
4. Do not change rulesets, thresholds or `ignoreFailures` to get a clean run
   unless the user agrees.
5. In the summary, say that lint passed and list any suppressions you added.

Suppression syntax, tools per repo and the rules each tool enforces:
**`docs/conventions/linting.md`**.
